# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ⚠ THE FIXTURES ARE BYTE-EXACT EVIDENCE, NOT TEXT, and git must not touch a
# byte of them.
#
# Each one is the exact sequence a named launch-monitor client puts on a
# socket, down to whether it ends with a newline — three of the sixteen
# clients delimit with '\n' and thirteen do not, and a framer must not care
# either way (tests/fixtures/README.md).  Without this line, git's end-of-line
# translation rewrites every '\n' as '\r\n' on a Windows checkout, so the
# suite there tests bytes no client ever sent.
#
# That is not hypothetical: it is what broke CI on the commit that made the
# conformance suite the gate.  CT-D24 walks every truncation of every fixture
# and caught it — the five files ending with '\n' decoded one byte later than
# the case allows.  Nothing else noticed, because a stray '\r' is legal JSON
# whitespace: every other case passed against the wrong bytes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/fixtures/*.json -text
